    "https://jcu.peopleadmin.com/postings/4242": {
      "title": "Lecturer (Part-Time), in Spanish and Hispanic Studies",
      "description": "John Carroll University Applicant Portal | Lecturer (Part-Time), in Spanish and Hispanic Studies Skip to Main Content Belong. Become. Be a Blue Streak. Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Lecturer (Part-Time), in Spanish and Hispanic Studies Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Job Title Lecturer (Part-Time), in Spanish and Hispanic Studies Rank Lecturer Tenure Information Non-Tenure Track Summary The Department of Ancient and Modern Languages and Cultures at John Carroll University invites applications for a Lecturer beginning spring semester 2027. We seek candidates who demonstrate commitment to excellent teaching. The teaching load for this position is one or two undergraduate Spanish language courses. Part-time faculty are paid on a per-credit-hour basis. The College of Arts & Sciences is home to the liberal arts and science programs that characterize John Carroll University’s nationally recognized Jesuit education. Consistent with the University’s mission, the Department of Ancient and Modern Languages and Cultures is committed to developing students into responsible citizens of the world. We offer instruction in six languages, plus courses in international cultures, leading to majors in Spanish and Ancient Greek and Roman Studies. Students may earn multi-age teacher licensure in Latin or Spanish, and major in International Business with French, German, Italian and Spanish or earn minors in French, German, and Italian. In keeping with the broader liberal arts mission of John Carroll University, the Spanish program seeks to prepare students to communicate effectively in Spanish, understand the cultural perspectives, products, and practices of the Spanish-speaking world, make connections between developments in Spanish-speaking cultures and trends in history, politics, and society, and act with intercultural competence. For its faculty, the Department of Ancient and Modern Languages and Cultures strives to offer a collegial and supportive working environment, including opportunities for professional development. Duties and Responsibilities Teaches using a proficiency-based approach to language learning. Follows the shared syllabus of the JCU Spanish and Hispanic Studies program and implements common assessments. Prepares and delivers course materials, in-class activities, and assessments consistent with course outcomes. Evaluates and grades students’ work in a timely manner. Maintains and submits student attendance records, grades and other required documentation by specified deadlines. Is available to assist students during office hours. Communicates regularly with Spanish section coordinator and department chair. Responds promptly to departmental and student communications. Meets periodically with supervisors and colleagues for collaboration, training and development. Participates in departmental efforts to assess student learning. Responds appropriately to the needs of a diverse population. Required Qualifications MA in Spanish, or a Master’s degree in Foreign Language Education with a specialization in Spanish, by time of hire, from a college or university accredited by the U.S. Department of Education or an internationally recognized college or university. ABDs and PhDs are also encouraged to apply. Applicants must have experience teaching Spanish to non-native speakers of Spanish. Native or near-native fluency in Spanish. Advanced communication skills in English and organizational skills. Ability to work professionally and effectively with minimal supervision. Sufficient technological skills to use the university’s course management system (Canvas) and any textbook-specific systems effectively. Preferred Qualifications Preference will be given to applicants who have experience teaching language and culture at the undergraduate level and/or using a content-based approach. Normal Work Location, Hours and Conditions Variable; classes are offered Monday/Wednesday/Friday mornings for 50 min. each or afternoons for 75 minutes; Tuesday/Thursday for 75 minutes each, typically during daytime hours. Applicant should indicate available days and times in the cover letter. About John Carroll University John Carroll University is a private, coeducational, Jesuit Catholic university, founded in 1886, dedicated to developing people with the knowledge and character to lead and to serve. The University is located in University Heights, Ohio, an attractive residential suburb 10 miles east of downtown Cleveland. Academically, the University consists of the College of Arts and Sciences, the College of Health and the Boler College of Business, which include graduate programs. The University offers more than 70 Academic Programs in the arts, social sciences, natural sciences, and business at the undergraduate level, and in select areas at the master’s level. The University enrolls approximately 2,500 undergraduate students and 500 graduate students and has a student-to-faculty ratio of 13:1. John Carroll University is one of 27 Jesuit universities in the United States and has been listed in U.S. News & World Report magazine’s top 10 rankings of Midwest regional universities for more than 30 consecutive years. Posting Detail Information Posting Number F265P Open Date Close Date Open Until Filled Special Instructions to Applicants The search committee will interview prospective candidates on campus. If appropriate, the candidate may be asked to teach a demo class before hire. For consideration, applicants should submit the application materials as soon as possible. Questions can be directed to Kris Ehrhardt, Chair of the Department of Ancient and Modern Languages and Cultures. EEO Statement We are an Equal Opportunity Employer. We welcome and value all individuals and encourage applications from people of all backgrounds, experiences, and perspectives. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Where did you first hear about the job opening? AJCU Alumni Referral Diversity Jobs Employee Referral Facebook Google Jobs Higher Ed Jobs I'm a Current JCU Employee Indeed Inside Higher Ed JCU Website LinkedIn Ohio Means Jobs Other NCAA The Chronicle of Higher Education Twitter/X If other, please specify (Open Ended Question) (Optional) Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Optional Documents Copyright 2025 © John Carroll University 1 John Carroll Boulevard, University Heights, Ohio, 44118 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jcu.peopleadmin.com/postings/4237": {
      "title": "Part-time Faculty in Psychology",
      "description": "John Carroll University Applicant Portal | Part-time Faculty in Psychology Skip to Main Content Belong. Become. Be a Blue Streak. Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Part-time Faculty in Psychology Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Job Title Part-time Faculty in Psychology Rank Lecturer Tenure Information Non-Tenure Track Summary The Department of Psychology in the College of Arts and Sciences invites applications for part-time faculty to teach core and elective undergraduate courses in psychology. Duties and Responsibilities Prepare course materials and pedagogy to achieve course learning goals and objectives. Employ appropriate pedagogy for the assigned courses. Conduct classes and deliver course material on assigned days and times. Utilize University Learning Management System ( LMS ) to deliver course information to students. Evaluate and grade student work in a timely manner. Maintain availability to students during posted hours to assist students. Respond in a timely manner to departmental and student communications. Meet periodically with supervisors and colleagues for collaboration, training, and development. Participate in departmental efforts to assess student learning. Respond appropriately to the needs of a diverse population. Required Qualifications A master’s or Ph.D. degree in psychology or a closely related field, from an accredited university is preferred. A commitment to outstanding teaching and delivering an excellent student experience is required. Preferred Qualifications Previous teaching experience at the university level is preferred. Normal Work Location, Hours and Conditions During the academic year, courses are taught on campus and face-to-face. Class times vary and instructors are expected to post available time for student questions outside of regular class hours. About John Carroll University John Carroll University is a private, coeducational, Jesuit Catholic university, founded in 1886, dedicated to developing people with the knowledge and character to lead and to serve. The University is located in University Heights, Ohio, an attractive residential suburb 10 miles east of downtown Cleveland. Academically, the University consists of the College of Arts and Sciences, the College of Health and the Boler College of Business, which include graduate programs. The University offers more than 70 Academic Programs in the arts, social sciences, natural sciences, and business at the undergraduate level, and in select areas at the master’s level. The University enrolls approximately 2,300 undergraduate students and 500 graduate students and has a student-to-faculty ratio of 13:1. John Carroll University is one of 27 Jesuit universities in the United States and has been listed in U.S. News & World Report magazine’s top 10 rankings of Midwest regional universities for more than 30 consecutive years. Posting Detail Information Posting Number F261P Open Date Close Date Open Until Filled Special Instructions to Applicants EEO Statement We are an Equal Opportunity Employer. We welcome and value all individuals and encourage applications from people of all backgrounds, experiences, and perspectives. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Where did you first hear about the job opening? AJCU Alumni Referral Diversity Jobs Employee Referral Facebook Google Jobs Higher Ed Jobs I'm a Current JCU Employee Indeed Inside Higher Ed JCU Website LinkedIn Ohio Means Jobs Other NCAA The Chronicle of Higher Education Twitter/X If other, please specify (Open Ended Question) (Optional) Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Optional Documents Copyright 2025 © John Carroll University 1 John Carroll Boulevard, University Heights, Ohio, 44118 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
